                <pb facs="0131" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg36"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.9315 Manchuria/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-03T17:00:00-05:00">February 3, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. Information received by the Department indicates that in some Soviet circles
                    there is an uneasy feeling that the outbreak of a conflict between Japan and the
                    Soviet Union in the spring or summer of this year is within the realm of
                    possibility.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
